## Lytics app — `create-job-and-authorization-for-data-and-insights-lytics`

Runs in **`https://app.lytics.com`** (not Contentstack).

- Flow: `projects/Data-and-Insights/set-up-data-insights/flows/create-job-and-authorization-for-data-and-insights-lytics.flow.json`
- Selectors: `.../create-job-and-authorization-for-data-and-insights-lytics.selectors.ts`
- Handlers: `actionRules.ts` — search **`create-job-and-authorization-for-data-and-insights-lytics`** / **`Lytics Job doc`**.
- Jobs list DOM snapshot: **`data/dom/Data-and-Insights/set-up-data-insights/lytics-joblistpage.html`**.

Headed smoke:

```bash
npm run test:data-and-insights:lytics-job-auth:headed
```

Env (see `.env.example`): optional **`LYTICS_APP_URL`** / **`LYTICS_APP_ORIGIN`** to override the app host; stack credentials and **`LYTICS_STACK_REGION`**. The flow opens **`https://app.lytics.com/`** then **Data Pipeline → Jobs** in the left nav (dedicated step in `actionRules.ts`). Use **`LYTICS_PIPELINE_JOBS_URL`** only if you switch the flow to deep-link. Requires a **saved Lytics session** (`use` is empty; no Contentstack login in this flow).

### Chained run: DAL OAuth then Lytics Job wizard (same browser)

Full **create-data-and-insights-lytics-integration** (with Contentstack `login`) runs first via `preflight.executeFlowBefore`, then **Import Entries job** steps continue in the **same context** — see `tests/data-and-insights-lytics-dal-then-job.spec.ts` and **`npm run test:data-and-insights:dal-then-lytics-job:headed`**. Optional: **`PW_KEEP_BROWSER_OPEN=1`** (Inspector pause at end). **`preflight.continueOnExecuteFlowBeforeFailure`** is set so the job steps still run if the DAL flow fails.

## Env (pick values that match visible stack / project names)

- `DAL_CONFIGURATION_DOMAIN` — domain field override  
- `DAL_CMS_STACK_SEARCH` — substring to filter **CMS Stacks** react-select, then pick a row whose **aria-label** matches when possible (`cs-org-lytics-tag-cms-stacks`). The flow step **`value`** (default **`AUTO`**) wins if set; else this env; else **`DEFAULT_STACK`**; else **`AUTO`**. Results load asynchronously — the runner polls briefly; use env for a stack name if no row matches **AUTO** in your org.
- `DAL_LAUNCH_PROJECT_SEARCH` — substring for **Launch Projects** (`cs-org-lytics-tag-launch-projects`). **Select this before Personalize**; if unset, **`DEFAULT_LAUNCH_PROJECT`** or the first visible row is used.  
- `DAL_PERSONALIZE_PROJECT_SEARCH` — substring for **Personalize Projects** (`cs-org-lytics-tag-personalize-projects`). If unset, the runner picks the **first visible** menu row (set this when multiple projects exist).  
- `DAL_LYTICS_ACCOUNT_SEARCH` — Lytics account dropdown filter (optional empty + Enter)

Example headed:

```bash
DAL_CMS_STACK_SEARCH=PriyalDocsStack DAL_PERSONALIZE_PROJECT_SEARCH=Test npm run test:data-and-insights:lytics-integration:headed
```

